      "character_start": 53313,
      "character_end": 53534,
      "utf8_byte_start": 53463,
      "utf8_byte_end": 53684,
      "literal": "For the reasons explained in Section 3 and 4.2 each subject took part in just one risk elicita-\n tion mechanism. In other words, the comparison of the risk aversion tasks was carried out in\n a pure between-subject design."
    },
    {
      "source_path": "private/risk_measure_working_0084/02.download.reading.txt",
      "source_sha256": "9cbfd32aaa698eeabe4ae871ac1c85490c0fe9d689c5aabfe03b0e6ebad0c5d3",
      "offset_convention": "zero-based, end-exclusive",
      "character_start": 76093,
      "character_end": 76238,
      "utf8_byte_start": 76277,
      "utf8_byte_end": 76422,
      "literal": "After performing the risk elicitation method, all subjects answered both the SOEP risk atti-\n tude question as well as the DOSPERT questionnaire."
    },
    {
      "source_path": "private/risk_measure_working_0084/02.download.reading.txt",
      "source_sha256": "9cbfd32aaa698eeabe4ae871ac1c85490c0fe9d689c5aabfe03b0e6ebad0c5d3",
      "offset_convention": "zero-based, end-exclusive",
      "character_start": 80398,
      "character_end": 80531,
      "utf8_byte_start": 80669,
      "utf8_byte_end": 80804,
      "literal": "Spearman’s coefficients, which simply rely upon the rank of choices and answers, finding\n an even lower significance of correlations."
    },
    {
      "source_path": "private/risk_measure_originals_0082/crosetto.crossref.json",
      "source_sha256": "8d5d701d4f24f367adc0698eac5d9f9c6d62244d9150072e144b1dba550d519f",
      "offset_convention": "zero-based, end-exclusive",
      "character_start": 1383,
      "character_end": 1486,
      "utf8_byte_start": 1383,
      "utf8_byte_end": 1486,
      "literal": "We run a replication experiment in a homogeneous subject pool using a between subjects one-shot design."
    },
    {
      "source_path": "private/risk_measure_originals_0082/csermely.xml",
      "source_sha256": "861af9753fc13d277f2d428faa2300406c34c2da99a8d15e6e8752bb4dd7dfdc",
      "offset_convention": "zero-based, end-exclusive",
      "character_start": 41184,
      "character_end": 41450,
      "utf8_byte_start": 41277,
      "utf8_byte_end": 41543,
      "literal": "We employed a within-subject design, meaning that each subject took decisions in each and every task as in other comparison studies (Eckel and Grossman <xref ref-type=\"bibr\" rid=\"CR41\">2008</xref>; Crosetto and Filippin <xref ref-type=\"bibr\" rid=\"CR31\">2016</xref>)."
